Import "../Chemistry.lingua"

Distinguish composition connectivity spatial structure and a sample (@chemistry-identity-levels: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Represent-molecular-connectivity-with-labels-and-justified-equivalences.lingua#r_007DFC5107CA477D570B05BDDC") { r_00B3E851A379503DEFF7CE20DC
Begin with a description of a material and ask what it actually specifies. A molecular formula gives numbers and kinds of atoms in an entity. A connectivity drawing proposes which atoms are bonded. A spatial model places those atoms in three dimensions. A sample can contain many entities, several species, a distribution of conformations and more than one phase. Identifying one of these levels does not automatically identify all the others.

Reuse [Read formulas and names without losing chemical identity](../general-chemistry/foundations/Formulas-names-and-charge.lingua#r_1CP96XH8H24BQWR2PEA3CT4H61), [Build a Lewis structure and test what it represents](../general-chemistry/bonding/Lewis-structures-and-valence.lingua#r_6H377ERVG3W7RTQBA71Y29FEMQ), [Distinguish formal charge, oxidation state, and delocalized bonding](../general-chemistry/bonding/Formal-charge-and-delocalization.lingua#r_43EAP1EC5N8J3HRPWV4D9T51AF), [Connect three-dimensional shape with polarity and behavior](../general-chemistry/bonding/Geometry-polarity-and-properties.lingua#r_1ESH4EFVR6399WYBN1405EJ38F) and [Check electron accounts before inferring charge distribution and molecular shape](Check-electron-accounts-before-inferring-charge-distribution-and-molecular-shape.lingua#r_0A6EA0B02E9CA642280AEA7D19). In the earlier carbonate example, several Lewis contributors describe one delocalized electronic account while retaining nuclear connectivity. They are not separately collected molecules switching between the drawings. In contrast, ethanol and dimethyl ether have the same molecular formula C₂H₆O but different atom connections. One places oxygen at the end of the heavy-atom chain with an O–H bond; the other places it between two carbons. Read the constitutional examples in [Organic Chemistry tenth edition by John McMurry](../sources/Organic-Chemistry-tenth-edition-by-John-McMurry.lingua#r_00F02946DB1C7E37631D69129A), section 3.2, for this distinction.

A skeletal drawing often suppresses carbon labels and attached hydrogens. Restore the atom and bond inventory before comparing two drawings. A corner or unlabeled line end represents carbon under the convention; heteroatoms and relevant hydrogens/charges need their stated notation. A condensed formula may express connections more specifically than a molecular formula. The same chain drawn bent, straight or from the opposite end can describe the same connectivity. A line crossing is not a bond unless the drawing says so.

The scope of a formula matters. An empirical formula gives a composition ratio rather than necessarily one molecule. A crystal formula unit is not automatically an isolated molecular entity. Isotope labeling, charge, electronic state and phase can matter to an identity question even when a simplified element count does not change. The finite molecular models in this block do not replace the later formation for ionic, metallic, polymeric or extended-network solids.

Structural identity is therefore a declared question. Are we comparing atom-labeled drawings, constitutional structures after arbitrary numbering is forgotten, conformations, configurations, or measured specimens? Define the equivalence allowed at that level before counting objects. Renumbering atoms is a change of description; breaking and forming bonds is a physical process with an energy and kinetic account. A computational map that merges descriptions is not evidence that a molecule can follow a corresponding physical path.

**Work:** restore the hydrogens in CH₃CH₂OH and CH₃OCH₃ and check that their molecular formulas agree while their oxygen neighbors differ. Draw one four-carbon chain three ways and give an explicit atom correspondence. Compare a molecular formula, a Lewis contributor, a spatial model and a mixture report by listing which questions each leaves unanswered. Use [Separate equivalence classes from ordering and reachability](../../mathematics/core/Separate-equivalence-classes-from-ordering-and-reachability.lingua#r_00844E60FB32CCD3D5D2D1B50D) for the meaning of equivalence, without requiring completion of all discrete mathematics before proceeding.

**Continue:** [Represent molecular connectivity with labels and justified equivalences](Represent-molecular-connectivity-with-labels-and-justified-equivalences.lingua#r_007DFC5107CA477D570B05BDDC).

**Return:** [Chemistry](../Chemistry.lingua#r_2NWJY1HCKPBM4T6YQSDHN8S3S0).
